ying":false,"_score_insider_buying":5.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Globalstar, Inc. provides mobile satellite services in the United States, Canada, Europe, Central and South America, and internationally. It offers duplex two-way voice and data products, including mobile voice and data services and equipment for remote business continuity, recreational usage, safety, emergency preparedness and response, and other applications. The company also provides data transmissions using a mobile or fixed device that transmits the location of the device and other information to a central monitoring station, including commercial IoT products; communication and data transmissions using SPOT family of devices, such as SPOT X, SPOT Gen4, and SPOT Trace that emergency alerts, and transmit messages and the location of the device; and voice communication and data transmissions. In addition, it offers commercial IoT devices to track assets comprising cargo containers and rail cars, monitor utility meters, and monitor oil and gas assets; small satellite transmitter modules, such as the STX-3, ST-150 and ST100, and chips that enable an integrator's products to access its network; engineering and other communication services using MSS and terrestrial spectrum licenses; and hardware and software designs to develop specific applications operating over satellite network, as well as the installation of gateways and antennas. It distributes its products through retailers and sales force, as well as www.findmespot.com e-commerce website. The company serves forestry, maritime, government, oil and gas, mining, leisure, emergency services, construction, and transportation sectors. Globalstar, Inc. was founded in 1993 and is headquartered in Covington, Louisiana.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Paul E. Jacobs Ph.D. | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $862,452 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 477 people. Revenue per employee of $572K ranks in the below the sector median among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.3M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $49K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Globalstar, Inc. is a large-cap communication services business with a $11.1B market cap on $273M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +7.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -0% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $616M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 226 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 59% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 127% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.2664701364237527},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (95% sell ratio, net $46.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Globalstar (GSAT) Stock Looks Stretched Following France C 3 Approval","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/globalstar-gsat-stock-looks-stretched-051453593.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795065293.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["regulatory"]},{"title":"(GSAT) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/GSAT_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_111726111201_1794931922.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794931922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Does France's Nod Mean for Globalstar (NASDAQ:GSAT) Satellites?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/communication/what-does-frances-nod-mean-for-globals